   710	excess 27.7%); removing them leaves 671,270 spectra against the reference implementation's 700,434, i.e. isotope-offset
   711	duplication accounts for the entire emission excess. But they are NOT mergeable: content cosine
   712	0.505 vs 0.446 for an arbitrary co-eluting neighbour (only 6.5% above 0.9), and every id-agnostic
   713	collapse rule loses 5,011-5,173 of 14,944 peptides (oracle still loses 1,387). "Keep the lightest" is
   714	backwards -- where only the heavy member is identified, Sage says the mass we reported was already
   715	correct 70% of the time. Mechanism: `findPartner` skips `used[]` peaks, so a leftover one step above a
   716	consumed run becomes its own monoisotope (heavy members carry fewer isotope partners, 3.53 vs 4.59).
