   745	Singly-charged precursor hypotheses are ~30% of emission and ~1.7% of peptides. A z=1 pseudo-spectrum
   746	is identified on 0.42% of its own spectra against 15.3% for z=2; tryptic peptides are essentially
   747	never 1+ in ESI and `charge:scoring count` breaks ties toward the LOW charge, so the mis-assignments
   748	land there. Dropping them removes their share of the multiple-testing burden too, so peptides go UP.
