   756	and below the 1.4% bound. Against the reference implementation, MSFragger goes 85.6 -> 86.7% (dataset D), 83.7 -> 88.3% (dataset A),
   757	91.8 -> 92.6% (dataset B); Sage on dataset D is 109.8% of the reference implementation. This is the first change in the emission line
   758	that improves both engines while cutting emission AND runtime.
