   572	  /// [cross-frame] Sliding-window aggregation of adjacent RT frames within ONE isolation window.
   573	  ///
   574	  /// the reference implementation sums "adjacent neighbor RT frames" of the same isolation window into a composite
   575	  /// (m/z x 1/K0) matrix BEFORE peak picking, which raises per-point S/N by ~sqrt(N) and lets weak
   576	  /// fragments form traces at all (Nat Commun 16:95 Methods). Because a diaPASEF isolation window is
   577	  /// sampled exactly ONCE per cycle, "adjacent frames" == adjacent CYCLES.
