   579	  /// SLIDING (stride 1), not block: block summing would divide our RT point count by N, and peaks here
   580	  /// span only 4-22 points, which would leave too few points to correlate at all. The cost of sliding
   581	  /// is that adjacent output points share input frames and are therefore AUTOCORRELATED, which inflates
   582	  /// Pearson r for signal and noise alike - the reason this must be benchmarked, not assumed.
