  1479	docs/reviews/window-loop-perf-2026-09-03/codex.md:138:Equal output counts do not imply equal work. Runtime is governed by raw points, detected features and candidate pairs, not the final number of spectra.
  1480	docs/reviews/window-loop-perf-2026-09-03/codex.md:144:2. **A specialized feature detector versus generic greedy MTD.** speXtractor invokes OpenMS `MassTraceDetection` separately over haloed bands at [DIAPseudoSpectra.cpp:919](/Users/kohlbach/Claude/speXtractor/src/DIAPseudoSpectra.cpp:919). The source itself records that increasing bands from 5 to 12 to 24 reduced trace CPU from 11,168 to 5,378 to 2,972 s because MTD candidate scanning is superlinear in band population at [DIAPseudoSpectra.cpp:2426](/Users/kohlbach/Claude/speXtractor/src/DIAPseudoSpectra.cpp:2426). That is an algorithmic red flag, not a mere compiler issue.
  1481	docs/reviews/window-loop-perf-2026-09-03/codex.md:146:3. **Fewer precursor hypotheses.** the reference implementation isotope-groups MS1 signals and discards peaks not belonging to a cluster. speXtractor assigns unsupported singleton traces a default charge unless an optional gate is enabled at [DIAPseudoSpectra.cpp:2096](/Users/kohlbach/Claude/speXtractor/src/DIAPseudoSpectra.cpp:2096). More precursor hypotheses mean proportionally more fragment scans and correlations.
  1482	docs/reviews/window-loop-perf-2026-09-03/codex.md:150:5. **Brute-force candidate association.** speXtractor indexes only by IM, then linearly scans that slice and tests RT before correlation at [DIAPseudoSpectra.cpp:1515](/Users/kohlbach/Claude/speXtractor/src/DIAPseudoSpectra.cpp:1515). A joint RT–IM feature index or feature-range intersection can avoid most candidate visits. The public the reference implementation paper does not disclose enough implementation detail to prove that it does so, but its retained m/z/IM signal ranges make it possible.
  1483	docs/reviews/window-loop-perf-2026-09-03/codex.md:152:6. **Correlation support representation.** speXtractor constructs a global ~1,300-point RT axis for every window, stores every fragment support, and repeatedly streams that support for every eligible precursor. the reference implementation correlates bounded precursor and fragment XIC features after feature segmentation. The paper does not publish sufficient low-level detail to quantify this difference, but it is a plausible major work reducer.
