  1621	docs/reviews/banding-halo-2026-09-03/vibe.md:8:The claim *"Traces cannot span more than trace:mass_error_ppm in m/z, so banding with a halo is exact"* (`src/DIAPseudoSpectra.cpp:909`, `src/DIAPseudoSpectra.cpp:1020-1021`) is **demonstrably false** for all three reasons you state. The code and comments themselves contain the evidence.
  1622	docs/reviews/banding-halo-2026-09-03/vibe.md:22:- **OpenMS MassTraceDetection behaviour:** Per your description and consistent with standard centroid-updating trace growth: each new peak within `mass_error_ppm` of the **current** centroid is accepted, and the centroid is **recomputed** to include it.
  1623	docs/reviews/banding-halo-2026-09-03/vibe.md:43:- **MassTraceDetection dependence:** Per your description, it is **greedy and order-dependent**, using an intensity-sorted apex list (`src/DIAPseudoSpectra.cpp:909`).
  1624	docs/reviews/banding-halo-2026-09-03/vibe.md:69:| **(c) Detect on whole window, parallelise differently** | **Yes** | **High** | Run MassTraceDetection on the full PeakMap without partitioning. Parallelise at a coarser grain: per-window (already done) or per-apex (would require rewriting MassTraceDetection's greedy loop into a task-parallel form). **Cost:** Likely a rewrite of OpenMS, which you forbade. |
