  1631	docs/reviews/banding-halo-2026-09-03/vibe.md:120:**Cost:** One full window at bands=1 is ~18 min / 160 GB. For a 24-window diaPASEF run, this is 18 min × 24/24 = **18 min** for one window plus negligible for banded versions.
  1632	docs/reviews/banding-halo-2026-09-03/vibe.md:122:**Honest reporting:** Add a log line: *"Banding approximation: X% trace set difference vs unbanded (window sample)"*
  1633	docs/reviews/banding-halo-2026-09-03/vibe.md:131:- **Current state:** `src/DIAPseudoSpectra.cpp:2033` shows the code now uses a **master/worker task pool**:
  1634	docs/reviews/banding-halo-2026-09-03/vibe.md:133:  // detectTraces_ distributes its bands as TASKS, which requires an enclosing parallel region;
  1635	docs/reviews/banding-halo-2026-09-03/vibe.md:135:- **Performance:** `src/DIAPseudoSpectra.cpp:2506-2510` shows banding **reduces total CPU** (11,168 → 2,972 s across 5/12/24 bands) because MassTraceDetection's cost is **superlinear** in peak count.
  1636	docs/reviews/banding-halo-2026-09-03/vibe.md:138:  - Banding is **not needed to fill cores** (task pool handles that)
  1637	docs/reviews/banding-halo-2026-09-03/vibe.md:141:  - **Cost:** No loss of parallelism; bands are tasks in the pool
  1638	docs/reviews/banding-halo-2026-09-03/vibe.md:144:**Answer:** Yes. The master/worker task pool (`src/DIAPseudoSpectra.cpp:1074-1075`, `src/DIAPseudoSpectra.cpp:2030-2040`) already decouples parallelism from banding. Bands are now **performance optimization**, not **parallelism mechanism**.
  1639	docs/reviews/banding-halo-2026-09-03/vibe.md:156:| **Measure error?** | **Jaccard vs unbanded** on stratified window sample; report symmetric difference. |
  1640	docs/reviews/banding-halo-2026-09-03/vibe.md:157:| **Parallelism without partition?** | **Yes** — task pool already supports it; bands are for performance, not parallelism. |
  1641	docs/reviews/banding-halo-2026-09-03/vibe.md:159:**The help text in `src/DIAPseudoSpectra.cpp:909` and `src/DIAPseudoSpectra.cpp:1020-1021` must be corrected:** it falsely claims exactness. Replace with: *"Banding partitions m/z into concurrent tasks with a 20×ppm halo to reduce per-thread work; results may vary slightly with band count."*
  1642	docs/reviews/backlog-2026-09-02-codex.md:1:1. **Blocker — B2 must precede landing A1.** The plan merges the parallel loader before diagnosing why batch 64 and 256 allegedly produce different content ([analysis:79–80](/Users/kohlbach/Claude/speXtractor/docs/BACKLOG-ANALYSIS-2026-09-02.md:79)). The stated exclusions are invalid: `const` does not prove library purity; absence of pointer-ordered containers in this file says nothing about OpenMS/opentims; and batch size changes OpenMP concurrency and which threads call `get_frame`, `decompress`, `save_to_buffs`, and `frame.close()` on one shared handle ([patch:209–240](/Users/kohlbach/Claude/speXtractor/patches/openms-brukertims-mz-calibration.patch:209)). Test batch 64 versus 256 at one thread, then 100 threads; checksum raw per-frame `(scan,intensity,mz,IM)` arrays before sorting/picking; then compare post-pick spectra. Correction: make B2 plan item 1 and prohibit A1 merge until raw-frame and stage digests identify or eliminate loader corruption.
  1643	docs/reviews/backlog-2026-09-02-codex.md:17:9. **Major — the active inventory misses R4 and the unresolved PTM ambiguity.** Double-scoring 2.99% of overlapping-window precursors remains an hours-scale 2–3% runtime item ([RUNTIME-QUALITY:21](/Users/kohlbach/Claude/speXtractor/docs/RUNTIME-QUALITY-ASSESSMENT-2026-07-27.md:21); [PROJECT-REVIEW:66–67](/Users/kohlbach/Claude/speXtractor/docs/PROJECT-REVIEW-2026-09-01.md:66)). The table-model result also leaves a 34.7%-versus-14% known-PTM ambiguity and an uninvestigated 1,610-unit Amidation bin ([dataset D-BASELINE:303–311](/Users/kohlbach/Claude/speXtractor/docs/dataset D-BASELINE.md:303)). Correction: add both as explicit open rows.
