  2062	docs/reviews/window-loop-perf-2026-09-03/kimi.err:66:  5. Correlation kernel raw work: score = 3753.6 window-wall-s ≈ 46%. The kernel correlates every fragment trace against every co-eluting precursor: loops over fragments in IM band (lo..hi from lower_bound on frag_im), RT gate, then dot over fragment support. With ~8.5M fragments/window... wait, "Fragment counts reach ~8.5 M per window" — that's fragment TRACES? The FragGrid comment says 8.5M fragments × ~510 support points. Hmm, 8.5M traces per window with 24 windows = 204M fragment traces total. And 932,491 precursor hypotheses / 24 ≈ 39k precursors per window. Score work per precursor = (IM-band fraction of fragments) × support length. delta_im = 0.01 over IM range [0.4,1.8] → if fragments uniformly spread, 0.02/1.4 = 1.4% of 8.5M = 121k candidates per precursor... times RT gate... That's 39k precursors × 121k = 4.7e9 candidate pairs per window, × 24 = 1.1e11 pairs. That's the raw work volume. IM distribution is not uniform (peptides cluster 0.6-1.1), so worse — maybe 5-10% of fragments in band.
