  2109	docs/reviews/window-loop-perf-2026-09-03/kimi.err:213:  Hmm — but careful: with 4 concurrent windows and 24 windows total, 6 waves; heaviest-first; the widest window = ~? If its window-wall is, say, 300+ s and total ~8,140/4 = 2,035 s min wall — currently 1,017 min at 8. Actually sum of window-wall CHANGES with band count (trace work falls): new sum ≈ mat 24 + trace ~2,200 + grid 396 + score 3,754×(25/12 better fill?) ≈ 6,400 → /4 = 1,600 s min wall vs current 1,017. WORSE unless score also speeds up (p_team 25 vs 12: score window-wall unchanged — it's the sum over windows of their own wall; score work per window same; sum same 3,754). Hmm wait — score window-wall per window is wall time of that stage; more threads per score region doesn't change the SUM over windows (each window's score wall = its work/threads... no!). Score stage wall per window = score_work / p_team. With p_team=25 vs 12, per-window score wall HALVES, sum → ~1,900. Trace with 24 bands: CPU 45% less, threads 24 vs 12 → wall per window = CPU_window/24 vs /12 with 55% less... trace wall sum → 3,965 × 0.55 × (12/24) ≈ 1,090?? Let me redo: trace CPU total T. Window i wall_i ≈ T_i/bands. Sum_i wall_i = T/bands. Current: T/12 = 3,965 → T ≈ 47,590?? But total CPU is 77,333 and trace can't use 47.6k at full fill... if inner fill in trace is f, CPU_trace = 12×3,965.6×f. With f unknown. For comparison purposes: new trace wall-sum = T' /24 where T' = 0.55T → 0.55×T/24 = 0.55×(3,965×12)/24 = 1,090 s (at same fill). New score sum = S_cpu/25 vs S_cpu/12 → 3,753.6×12/25 = 1,802 s. Grid 396 (serial, unchanged — or parallelised). New total window-wall-sum ≈ 24 + 1,090 + 396 + 1,802 ≈ 3,312 s / 4 slots = 828 s + tail losses. vs current 1,139. Potential -27%! If fill holds. But 4 slots × tail: heavy-first biggest window: its wall ≈ (its trace/24 + its score/25) — big window wall might be ~150-250 s, fine. This could be the single biggest CHEAP win. But memory: 4 windows in flight → peak ~55+4×12×(T' scale)...