  1408	   376	  /// [compact] Quantised frame store for the per-window buffer.
  1409	   377	  ///
  1410	   378	  /// Holding all 24 isolation windows as full OpenMS PeakMaps costs ~89 GB resident before any window
  1411	   379	  /// is consumed, which is what forces `max_concurrent_windows` down and caps our parallelism at ~7
  1412	   380	  /// cores (the reference implementation uses ~43). A frame only needs (m/z, intensity, 1/K0) per peak plus one RT, so we
  1413	   381	  /// store structure-of-arrays with quantised keys and materialise a PeakMap ONLY inside the worker
  1414	   382	  /// that is about to trace it, freeing the compact copy immediately.
  1415	   383	  ///
  1416	   384	  /// Precision (deliberately far finer than every downstream tolerance, so tracing is unaffected):
  1417	   385	  ///   m/z : uint32 at 1e-5 Da  -> 0.007 ppm at m/z 1400, vs a 20 ppm trace tolerance (2800x margin)
  1418	   386	  ///   1/K0: uint16 over [0.4,1.8] -> 2.1e-5, vs a 0.01 IM tolerance (470x margin)
