  1534	   502	  /// [stream] Pick-and-compact consumer: removes the one-shot-read memory floor.
  1535	   503	  ///
  1536	   504	  /// MEASURED: `loadExperiment` reaches 90.3 GB RSS / 99.0 GB peak at t=0s, BEFORE any compaction
  1537	   505	  /// exists — so the compact store (10 B/peak, 20.9 GB for 2.19e9 peaks) can never lower the peak.
  1538	   506	  /// The floor is the whole run being resident at once. BrukerTimsFile::loadDIAStreaming hands us one
  1539	   507	  /// frame at a time, so we peak-pick and compact each frame on arrival and never hold the raw run.
  1540	   508	  ///
  1541	   509	  /// Windows are keyed by the SAME (lo,hi) isolation-window key used downstream, taken from the
  1542	   510	  /// spectrum's own precursor, so routing is identical to the old split - not by swath_nr, whose
  1543	   511	  /// ordering is the reader's business and need not match ours.
