   161	  Question 4: the reference implementation 3.1× cheaper CPU. Algorithmic differences:
   162	  1. Frame summing before peak picking (the reference implementation core): sums ~5 adjacent cycles into composite (m/z,IM) frames → 5× fewer point observations to trace, and higher S/N means the noise threshold kills more junk → dramatically fewer fragment traces. speXtractor traces RAW frames at noise 10 → 8.5M traces/window. Trace count drives BOTH trace-stage and score-stage work superlinearly (score work ∝ precursors × candidate fragments).
