  2370	  /// Build a pseudo-MS2 from a fragment list (m/z,intensity) + ranking scores: keeps top
  2371	  /// max_frags by score, drops if < min_frags, annotates the synthetic precursor. Deterministic.
  2372	  /// EXPORT-TIME CALIBRATION. On a flight-time axis the measured quantity is a bin; m/z is a
  2373	  /// calibrated function of it and of the frame's digitizer temperature. Applying that function
  2374	  /// ONCE, here, when the value is written, is what keeps the reported mass free of anything the
  2375	  /// intermediate gates did in cached m/z space -- and the apex frame's own factor is the most
  2376	  /// accurate one to use. A zero bin means the trace came from the OpenMS detector, which has no
  2377	  /// bin, and the value it computed stands.
