commit 3a1d91e76fc6ff2d2e7aa859bea84278214bad07
Author:     Oliver <oliver.kohlbacher@uni-tuebingen.de>
AuthorDate: Fri Sep 4 06:13:48 2026 +0200
Commit:     Oliver <oliver.kohlbacher@uni-tuebingen.de>
CommitDate: Fri Sep 4 06:13:48 2026 +0200

    Trace profiles are spans, not point lists: entry frame + intensities in a per-store arena
    
    A trace point has one degree of freedom -- its intensity -- so the three parallel 4-byte vectors
    (frame, intensity, bin) and their three mallocs per trace are replaced by (frame0, off, len, npts,
    apex) into a per-window/per-MS1 arena, zero meaning missing. Entry frames are STORE-LOCAL because a
    window's consecutive frames are ~13 apart on the global axis. Every consumer walks REAL points in
    frame order, so the floating-point sums are visited exactly as before: the change is meant to be
    pure representation and is gated on a byte-identical spectrum digest for BOTH detectors.
    
    FragGrid (a CSR copy of every profile) is replaced by FragStats: G as the count of frames carrying
    a real fragment point, per-fragment mean/invnorm over real points, and the MS1->window nearest-frame
    table through both frame tables. The scorer's inner loop is two sequential streams. Band and chunk
    tasks append to private stores that the window absorbs after each join, rebasing offsets, per the
    reviewed sequencing (docs/TRACE-STRUCT-REDESIGN.md, revision 2).
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

