commit 6ea4e3f59068ed5b13ec8905d113d9b746727b63
Author:     Oliver <oliver.kohlbacher@uni-tuebingen.de>
AuthorDate: Fri Sep 4 06:32:25 2026 +0200
Commit:     Oliver <oliver.kohlbacher@uni-tuebingen.de>
CommitDate: Fri Sep 4 06:32:25 2026 +0200

    Span refactor: a split child's bin comes from its own apex peak, not from a parent lookup
    
    The OpenMS arm was digest-identical after the span refactor while the integer arm lost 3.3% of
    peptides, which localises the fault to integer-only code. It was the parent walk added in
    splitIntegerTraces: parents within a chunk are ordered by IM and m/z, not by frame, and their frame
    ranges overlap freely, so a child could be attributed to the wrong parent and given another trace's
    flight-time bin. The pre-span code never did this -- the bin travelled inside the MassTrace as each
    peak's m/z -- and that is restored.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

