Author:     Oliver <oliver.kohlbacher@uni-tuebingen.de>
AuthorDate: Thu Sep 3 19:00:33 2026 +0200
Commit:     Oliver <oliver.kohlbacher@uni-tuebingen.de>
CommitDate: Thu Sep 3 19:00:33 2026 +0200

    Score gate reads a parallel array, not the 96-byte trace record
    
    The gate rejects 99.4% of the fragments it visits and needed one field to do it. Reading that field
    out of the Trace made the scan stride 96 B for 8 B of payload: an estimated 83 TB of memory traffic
    per dataset D run, against 6.9 TB for a parallel array. The record is now touched only by survivors.
    
    Output-neutral: the same fragments are visited in the same order and the same ones pass.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
