commit 436f3c6ab0f247d49bc362dfccfb9fc76414c221
Author:     Oliver <oliver.kohlbacher@uni-tuebingen.de>
AuthorDate: Thu Sep 3 18:27:52 2026 +0200
Commit:     Oliver <oliver.kohlbacher@uni-tuebingen.de>
CommitDate: Thu Sep 3 18:27:52 2026 +0200

    Use the instrument's flight-time index, not a uniform m/z grid
    
    The tool only runs on ion-mobility TOF data, so the native axis is always there. It is lossless (the
    bin IS the measurement, not a quantisation of a derived quantity), ~340x smaller, and the same ion
    gives the same bin in every frame -- whereas a calibrated m/z wobbles with the digitizer
    temperature, so an m/z-space tolerance spends part of itself absorbing calibration drift.
    
    The extraction now never needs a calibrated m/z: grouping, gating and correlation are in bins, and
    TdfMzCalibration is applied once per trace at report time with the apex frame's own factor. The
    tolerance in bins is derived by converting both ends through the calibration, not by assuming
    m ~ tof^2. Without the vendor calibration there is no axis and the detector refuses to run.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
