    32	  are EXACT; n=1 is justified for both. CONSEQUENCE: the MSFragger k-curve non-monotonicity
    33	  (11,402/11,560/11,482/11,751 across k=1..4) is NOT run-to-run noise -- it is a REAL (non-smooth)
    34	  response to the different inputs (codex called this in review; now measured). The earlier "MSFragger
    35	  is a noisy guardrail" framing was WRONG on the noise: MSFragger numbers are exact, just non-monotonic
    36	  in k (its optimum k differs from Sage's). The ONLY stochastic uncertainty in the whole benchmark is
    37	  the entrapment FDR estimate (small n), which the bootstrap CI below now quantifies.
